# prompt: car engine idling loop
# tags: engine, idle, car, loop
# The firing order is a delay line, not a sequence of notes: one sub thump
# recirculated every 55 ms is about eleven pulses a second, which is a
# four-cylinder at idle. Feedback is kept at 0.5 rather than the rotor's 0.88
# because the tail has to die inside the loop period, or the seam is audible.
sound "engine idle" 950ms cycle loop
  chug: sub ~55Hz[35..90] >> delay ~55ms[30..110] feedback 0.5 mix 1 | gain 0.4 decay 40ms
  rumble: noise brown >> lp ~500Hz[200..1200] | gain 0.3 attack 100ms decay 800ms
  whir: tone saw ~180Hz[90..380] >> lp ~800Hz[300..2000] | gain 0.12 attack 150ms decay 700ms
